# Stream-scoped persistent sessions on multiplexed transports (issue #5351).
#
# The connection-scoped multi-request persistent-session model (a handler that
# calls setPersistent() and parks a dedicated handler thread on the connection
# for its lifetime) is an HTTP/1.x carry-over that is WRONG for HTTP/2 and
# HTTP/3: those connections multiplex many independent streams and are pooled /
# reused, so the connection-close that ends an H1 session never arrives.  The
# parked thread could then only be released by a best-effort end-of-session
# request; if that was lost on a pooled connection the thread stayed parked
# forever and its thread-local resources (e.g. an open DB transaction) leaked —
# exhausting datasource pools downstream.
#
# The fix binds a persistent session to a single bidirectional stream whose
# lifecycle (END_STREAM / RST_STREAM / RESET_STREAM+STOP_SENDING /
# connection-close) is transport-deterministic and reliably delivered.  On
# multiplexed transports the framework therefore no longer parks a dedicated
# thread for a connection-scoped session: a handler that opts into persistence
# is released immediately after its response, its thread-local context torn down
# deterministically — it cannot leak.  A genuine cross-request session on H2/H3
# must instead be expressed as a single bidirectional streaming request (the
# body_streaming / extended-CONNECT path, exercised by Http2BidiStreaming.qtest
# and the QUIC WebSocket tests), whose teardown rides the same stream lifecycle.
#
# This test verifies:
#  - a multiplexed handler that calls setPersistent() is torn down promptly and
#    exactly once (persistentClosed() fires) without any stream reset, idle TTL,
#    or connection close — i.e. no parked thread, no leak (the core regression);
#  - the listener stays healthy across many such sessions on reused connections;
#  - destroying the server is clean (no crash) whether or not a session is live.
#
# HTTP/1.x retains the connection-scoped model (there connection == stream, which
# is already correct) and is covered by HttpServer.qtest / HttpServerStreamCallback.qtest.

%modern

%prepend-module-path "${SCRIPT_DIR}/../../../../qlib"
%requires Util
%requires HttpServerUtil
%requires HttpServer
%requires RestClient
%requires RestClientIo
%requires HttpClientIo
%requires Mime
%requires Logger
%requires QUnit

%exec-class HttpServerMultiplexedPersistentTeardownTest

